  "id": "COMPOUND:47 - DISEASE:2012",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between rasburicase and Menstruation disorder NOS, mediated through its effect on DNA fragmentation factor subunit beta. This mechanism is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that rasburicase influences this protein, which in turn contributes to the development of the condition. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible pathway, with rasburicase acting as a modulator of DNA fragmentation factor subunit beta, which is linked to the pathophysiology of Menstruation disorder NOS. The evidence is robust in its connectivity and directionality, though the exact nature of the interaction between rasburicase and DNA fragmentation factor subunit beta remains to be fully elucidated. The observed association is further strengthened by the shared role of this protein in hematologic diseases, reinforcing the potential relevance of rasburicase in this context.",
